You are extracting ONLY the core module metadata from a D&D 5e adventure PDF.

STRICT RULES:
- Output JSON ONLY
- Do not include any keys other than those listed
- Do not describe locations, NPCs, items, or plot
- Do not infer beyond explicit or strongly implied text

Return EXACTLY this JSON structure:

ID RULES (MANDATORY):
- All IDs must be lowercase ASCII
- Format: <entity>.<slug>[.<context>]
- Slugs use underscores only
- IDs must be stable and deterministic
- If a collision occurs, append .2, .3, etc
- Never reuse an ID for a different entity

{
  "module": {
    "id": "string-id-slug",
    "title": "Full Adventure Title",
    "subtitle": "Optional subtitle or null",
    "edition": "5e",
    "recommended_levels": "e.g. 1–3",
    "starting_area": "area_id",
    "summary": "1–2 sentence neutral overview"
  }
}

Use null where data is not present.
